---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const title = "PelliScope Europe | Privacy notice";
const description = "Privacy information for the PelliScope European website and services.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical="https://pelliscope.eu/privacy.html">
  <Header />
  <main id="main-content" class="legal-main">
    <section class="legal-hero section-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span></span>European operation · Last updated 26 July 2026</p>
      <h1>Privacy, explained<br /><em>without shortcuts.</em></h1>
      <p>
        This notice applies to the PelliScope European website and services operated by HawkFranklin OÜ.
        A specific clinic or clinician may provide an additional notice before clinical information is shared.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="legal-layout section-shell">
      <aside class="legal-summary">
        <strong>Operator</strong>
        <p>HawkFranklin OÜ<br />Registry code 17558108<br />Ahtri tn 12, 15551 Tallinn, Estonia</p>
        <a href="mailto:contact@hawkfranklin.in">contact@hawkfranklin.in</a>
      </aside>
      <article class="legal-copy">
        <section>
          <h2>1. Scope and roles</h2>
          <p>
            HawkFranklin OÜ is responsible for this website and for personal data it collects for European service
            registration, inquiries and platform operation. When clinical care is requested, the participating
            clinician or clinic may act as an independent controller for its professional record and clinical
            decisions. The relevant roles will be identified at the point of collection.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>2. Information we may collect</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Contact and account information supplied for an inquiry or service registration.</li>
            <li>Professional credentials, registration number and issuing jurisdiction supplied by clinicians.</li>
            <li>Technical and security information needed to deliver and protect the website or service.</li>
            <li>Photographs, symptom context and other health information only when a user deliberately submits a case.</li>
            <li>Consent, access and audit records associated with protected clinical workflows.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>3. Why information is used</h2>
          <p>
            Information may be used to answer inquiries, manage service access, verify professional eligibility,
            organise a user-submitted case, protect the service, meet legal obligations and—only in an active
            jurisdiction—support a requested clinician consultation. The legal basis depends on the specific
            interaction and will be identified where additional information is collected.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>4. Clinical information and sharing</h2>
          <p>
            A screening result is informational and is not a diagnosis. When a visitor explicitly accepts the
            Community permission in the website’s Try Now flow, sanitized photographs and the AI screening result
            are stored in a protected moderation queue. They are not published to the Doqlin partner service until
            an authorized PelliScope administrator approves that specific packet. Other patient cases are not sent
            to a clinician or Community merely because they have been prepared; the user must choose or consent to
            the applicable sharing path.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>5. Service providers and international access</h2>
          <p>
            Technical providers may process data where necessary to operate or secure the service. Any international
            transfer of protected personal data must use an applicable legal mechanism and safeguards. A production
            service notice will identify material providers and transfer arrangements before live clinical use.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>6. Retention and security</h2>
          <p>
            Information is retained only for the relevant service, safety, contractual and legal purposes. Exact
            retention periods depend on whether information is an inquiry, account record, service record or clinical
            record and will be stated in the applicable service notice. We use technical and organisational controls,
            but no online system can promise absolute security.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            Subject to applicable law, you may request access, correction, deletion, restriction, portability or
            object to certain processing. You may also withdraw consent where consent is the basis used, without
            affecting earlier lawful processing. Contact us at the address above. You may complain to your relevant
            data-protection authority.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>8. Children, emergencies and updates</h2>
          <p>
            PelliScope Europe is not offered as an unsupervised service for children and is not an emergency service.
            Seek local emergency assistance for urgent symptoms. We may update this notice as country
            services and technical arrangements are defined; the date at the top records the current version.
          </p>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
